-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/c6446243-5fbe-58f6-8d2b-abd3b055c729
-- title:
--   Level-one torus quotient is a form of 𝔽ₚ[(ℤ/p)^t]
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $p$ is a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ (`hpM`) and $p^2 \nmid M$ (`hpM2`), with $M/p$ nonzero, and $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ is a subgroup which, by `hHp`, contains every unit whose image under the reduction `ZMod.unitsMap` $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial. Further, `Pl` is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit in it (`hPl`, the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), whose residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField Pl` has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed and is regarded as a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra; and `hj` states that the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` of $j$ lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral form ratios at full level.
--
--   **Model and Néron object.** $\mathfrak{X}$ is a datum `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` (a Deligne–Rapoport-style integral model package at $p$ for the two-chart models `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` and `toBase p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj` over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the base ring `R p`, together with a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` and its comparison data). $\Lambda$ is a `JHNeronObjectAtP.LevelData p M H hpM Pl` and $O$ a `JHNeronObjectAtP p M H hpM Pl hPl Λ`: a smooth, separated, surjective relative group scheme $O.g : O.G \to \operatorname{Spec}$(base ring) with commutative relative group law $O.L$, a bijection `O.pts` between $J_H(M) =$ `JH M H` $= \operatorname{Pic}^0$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` and the sections over the generic point, Hecke operators, and a toric rank $t := O.\mathtt{toricRank}$.
--
--   **Representability hypotheses.** `hrep` asserts that the type `RepresentsRelSubPic` is nonempty for the curve `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` rigidified along $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$, for the subfunctor condition `algEquivZeroCut` (a rigidified line bundle is admitted when, on every geometric fibre, it is algebraically equivalent to zero), and for the designation of a relative $\operatorname{Pic}^0$ given by $O.G$, $O.g$ and the unit section $O.L.\mathtt{one}$ at the identity of $\operatorname{Spec}($`R p`$)$: that is, a Poincaré rigidified bundle satisfying the condition, universal among such bundles on arbitrary bases, and trivial along the zero section. `hrepΛ` asserts the same for the curve `toBase p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj` with the section $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\pi$, and for the designation given by $\Lambda.X$, $\Lambda.f$ and $\Lambda.L.\mathtt{one}$.
--
--   **The henselian local ring.** $R_h$ is a henselian local domain, an algebra over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with faithful action (so that $R_h \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is injective), subject to: `hRA`, every $x \in R_h$ maps into `Pl`; `hRloc`, $x$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R_h$ precisely when the `Pl`-valuation of its image is $< 1$. Moreover $R_h$ carries a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra structure with `hres`: $x$ maps to $0$ in $\mathbb{Z}/p$ precisely when the valuation of its image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is $< 1$.
--
--   **The $p$-divisible group and the comparison maps.** $\mathcal{G}$ is a [`PDivisibleGroup Rh p h`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199): a tower of finite free cocommutative Hopf $R_h$-algebras $\mathcal{G}.\mathtt{level}\,v$ with surjective transition bialgebra maps, $\operatorname{rank} = p^{vh}$, and kernel of the $v$-th transition equal to the $p^v$-torsion ideal. $\Delta$ is an additive map from $\mathcal{G}.\mathtt{Points}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ (the direct limit of the convolution groups of $R_h$-algebra characters at each level) to $J_H(M)$, and $e$ a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-linear map of Tate modules $T_p(\mathcal{G}.\mathtt{Points}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})) \to T_p(J_H(M))$, where [`TateModule p A`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15) consists of sequences $(x_n)$ with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$. The hypotheses on this pair are: `hΔinj`, $\Delta$ is injective; `hΔlev`, for every $v$ an element $y$ of $J_H(M)$ lies in $O.\mathtt{finPts}(p^v)$ — the subgroup generated by the $p^v$-torsion divisor classes that extend to the place, in the sense of `ExtendsToPlace Pl Λ.σA` — exactly when $y = \Delta$ of (the image of) some level-$v$ point; `hΔgal`, $\Delta$ is equivariant for $\tau \in \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ and $\tau'$ an $R_h$-automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ agreeing with it pointwise; `hΔhecke`, for every set $S$ and every Hecke generator $g \in$ [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) there is a system $\varphi_v$ of $R_h$-bialgebra endomorphisms of the levels, compatible with the transitions, inducing on $\Delta$-images the operator `genOpH M H S g`; `he`, the $n$-th component of $e(x)$ is $\Delta$ of the $n$-th component of $x$; `heinj`, $e$ is injective; `herange`, $y$ lies in the range of $e$ exactly when each component $y_n$ lies in $O.\mathtt{finPts}(p^n)$; `hegal`, $e$ intertwines the Tate-module action `𝒢.tateModuleRep` of $\tau'$ with `JH.tateGaloisRep` of $\tau$; `hsat`, the range of $e$ is $p$-saturated; `hcoker`, the quotient $T_p(J_H(M))/\operatorname{range} e$ is $\mathbb{Z}_p$-linearly isomorphic to $\mathbb{Z}_p^{t}$; `htor`, every element of $O.\mathtt{toricPts}(p^v)$ (the subgroup generated by the range of $O.\mathtt{toricPoint}$) is $\Delta$ of a level-$v$ point.
--
--   **The quotient $p$-divisible group.** $\mathcal{B}$ is a [`PDivisibleGroup Rh p hB`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199), $\psi_v : \mathcal{B}.\mathtt{level}\,v \to \mathcal{G}.\mathtt{level}\,v$ are $R_h$-bialgebra maps, and $h'$ is a natural number, with the numerical relations `hhB`: $h = t + h_{\mathcal{B}}$, and `hhB2`: $h_{\mathcal{B}} = 2h'$. The hypotheses on $\psi$ are: `hψt`, compatibility with the transitions; `hψker`, for a level-$v$ point $x$ of $\mathcal{G}$, the point of $\mathcal{B}$ obtained by composing its character with $\psi_v$ is trivial exactly when $\Delta(x) \in O.\mathtt{toricPts}(p^v)$; `hψsurj`, every level-$v$ point of $\mathcal{B}$ arises in this way from a level-$v$ point of $\mathcal{G}$; `hψred`, if the $\psi_v$-image of $x$ reduces to the identity (its character agrees with the counit composed with $R_h \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ up to valuation $< 1$ on every element), then so does $x$ itself; `hperiod`, for every $v$, every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup `Pl.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, every $p^v$-torsion class $z$ in $\operatorname{Pic}^0$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` and every level-$v$ point $y$ with $\Delta(y) = \sigma \cdot z - z$, the $\psi_v$-image of $y$ reduces to the identity in the same valuation-theoretic sense.
--
--   **The embedding into the Néron object.** $\rho_h :$ `R p` $\to R_h$ is a ring map and $\iota_v : \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{G}.\mathtt{level}\,v) \to O.G$ a family of morphisms, subject to: `hρh`, $\rho_h$ followed by $R_h \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structural map of `R p`; `hιbase`, $\iota_v$ followed by $O.g$ factors as $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R_h \to \mathcal{G}.\mathtt{level}\,v$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec} \rho_h$; `hιcl`, the resulting map into the fibre product of $O.g$ and $\operatorname{Spec} \rho_h$ is a closed immersion; `hιp`, $\iota_v$ followed by multiplication by $p^v$ for $O.L$ equals its base map followed by the unit section; `hιpts`, for a level-$v$ point $x$ the section $O.\mathtt{pts}(\Delta(x))$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the character of $x$ followed by $\iota_v$; `hιmul`, for every $R_h$-algebra $B$ and level-$v$ points $x, y$ over $B$ lying over the base (as expressed by the two hypotheses `hx`, `hy`), the morphism attached to $x \cdot y$ is the $O.L$-product of those attached to $x$ and $y$; `hιt`, compatibility of $\iota$ with the transitions; `hιhecke`, for every Hecke generator $g$ there is a system $\varphi_v$ of $R_h$-bialgebra endomorphisms, compatible with the transitions, with $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi_v$ followed by $\iota_v$ equal to $\iota_v$ followed by $O.\mathtt{hecke}\,S\,g$, and inducing `genOpH M H S g` on $\Delta$-images; `hιfin`, for every $v$, granted the factorisations `h3` and `h4`, the canonical morphism $j_v$ from $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{G}.\mathtt{level}\,v)$ to the base change along $\operatorname{Spec} \rho_h$ of the $p^v$-torsion subscheme of $O.G$ (the fibre product of multiplication by $p^v$ and the unit section) is both an open immersion and a closed immersion, and every point of that base change lying over the closed point of $R_h$ is in the range of $j_v$ on underlying spaces.
--
--   **The torus-quotient tower.** `hjB` requires that for every $v$ the map $\mathbb{Z}/p \otimes_{R_h} \psi_v$, i.e. `Bialgebra.TensorProduct.map (BialgHom.id (ZMod p) (ZMod p)) (ψ v)`, be injective. Finally $T : \mathbb{N} \to \mathrm{Type}$ is a family of commutative rings, each a cocommutative Hopf algebra over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ that is finite and free as a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-module, with $\mathbb{Z}/p$-bialgebra maps $t_{T,v} : T(v+1) \to T(v)$ and $\pi_{T,v} : \mathbb{Z}/p \otimes_{R_h} \mathcal{G}.\mathtt{level}\,v \to T(v)$, subject to: `htT`, each $t_{T,v}$ is surjective; `hrankT`, $\dim_{\mathbb{Z}/p} T(v) = p^{vt}$; `hkerT`, the kernel of $t_{T,v}$ is the $p^v$-torsion ideal [`PDivisibleGroup.Hopf.torsionIdeal (ZMod p) (T (v+1)) (p^v)`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L157); `hπT`, each $\pi_{T,v}$ is surjective; `hπTt`, $\pi_{T,v}$ precomposed with $\mathbb{Z}/p \otimes \mathcal{G}.\mathtt{transition}\,v$ equals $t_{T,v}$ composed after $\pi_{T,v+1}$; `hexT`, the kernel of $\pi_{T,v}$ is the ideal generated by the image, under $\mathbb{Z}/p \otimes \psi_v$, of the augmentation ideal (the kernel of the counit) of $\mathbb{Z}/p \otimes_{R_h} \mathcal{B}.\mathtt{level}\,v$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** The type of $\kappa$-bialgebra isomorphisms
--   $$\kappa \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p} T(1) \;\simeq\; \kappa \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p} (\mathbb{Z}/p)\bigl[(\mathbb{Z}/p)^{t}\bigr]$$
--   is nonempty, where the right-hand factor is the additive monoid algebra `AddMonoidAlgebra (ZMod p) (Fin O.toricRank → ZMod p)` and $t = O.\mathtt{toricRank}$.
--
--   The statement identifies the level-one stage of the torus-quotient tower of the finite part of the Néron object of $J_H(M)$ at a place above $p$, for $p$ exactly dividing $M$: after base change to the algebraically closed residue field it becomes the group algebra of $(\mathbb{Z}/p)^t$, $t$ the toric rank, so that its spectrum is the $t$-fold product of $\mu_p$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_verschiebung_bialgEquiv_torusQuotient_finPts_jHNeronObjectAtP_of_finPtsWitness`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_verschiebung_bialgEquiv_torusQuotient_finPts_jHNeronObjectAtP_of_finPtsWitness), where the Verschiebung of each stage of the tower is shown to be an isomorphism, in the analysis of the $p$-torsion of the Jacobian at a prime of multiplicative reduction that underlies level lowering.
